  }
 ],
 "_comment_copy_atom": [
  "make_copy_atom(op, dtype, num_bits_per_copy) -> Copy_Atom whose ValLayout is",
  "(1, num_bits/dtype_bits):(0,1). Checks ui.js's DTYPE_BITS table against the DSL.",
  "The six SIMT Ops -- CopyUniversalOp, cpasync.CopyG2SOp and the four",
  "directional CopyG2ROp / CopyR2GOp / CopyS2ROp / CopyR2SOp -- all produce a",
  "byte-identical Atom, so every case here is checked against the SAME",
  "(1,N):(0,1) expectation. The directional cases mirror universal ones at the",
  "same widths on purpose: that identity is the reason make_copy_atom,",
  "make_tiled_copy and make_tiled_copy_tv can share one Op table (ui.js's",
  "SIMT_COPY_OPS), and it is checked here rather than assumed.",
  "The `attrs` cases pin the tab's claim that the directional Ops' memory",
  "attributes change the MLIR atom type and the emitted PTX but NOT the layouts:",
  "run.js checks them against the same (1,N):(0,1) expectation as everything",
  "else. They also document three cross-parameter rules the DSL enforces (found",
  "by writing these cases and watching them fail): `invariant` requires every",
  "other memory feature at its default; `load_cache_mode` must be ALWAYS and",
  "`store_cache_mode` WRITE_BACK unless `memory_order` is WEAK."
 ],
