 "_comment_mma_atom": [
  "make_mma_atom(op) for the three DENSE cute.nvgpu.warp WarpMmaOp subclasses.",
  "Oracle: cutlass.cute -- thr_id, shape_mnk, and tv_layout_A/B/C, each with",
  "size/cosize and its value at every point of the domain.",
  "Ported by tabs/make_mma_atom.js:mmaWarpAtom, which is a TABLE rather than a",
  "derivation -- CUTLASS itself defines these as hand-written MMA_Traits",
  "specializations (include/cute/atom/mma_traits_sm80.hpp:78), so there is no",
  "arithmetic to port and the only way to be right is to diff every entry.",
  "The corpus is EXHAUSTIVE over the valid parameter domains (16 cases). That is",
  "what pins the tab's load-bearing claim that the three layouts depend only on",
  "the Op family and K: 16 combinations collapse to 6 distinct layout triples, so",
  "neither ab_dtype nor acc_dtype provably changes anything.",
  "Excluded on purpose: MmaF16BF16SparseOp, the fourth WarpMmaOp subclass -- it",
  "traces fine, but MmaAtom exposes no metadata (E) layout and its A layout is",
  "over the LOGICAL (M,K) tile, so the tab could not draw what distinguishes it.",
  "Also MmaMXF4Op / MmaMXF8Op / MmaMXF4NVF4Op / MmaMXF8F6F4Op, which subclass",
  "MmaOp rather than WarpMmaOp and are sm_120-only, so no oracle could be",
  "generated for them here -- an untested tab entry is worse than a missing one."
 ],
