 "_comment_tma_partition": [
  "tma_partition(atom, 0, Layout<1>, sT, gT). The generator runs the real pipeline",
  "(make_tiled_tma_atom -> group_modes / zipped_divide -> tma_partition) and records",
  "both the partitioned results AND the grouped tensor strings it fed in, so the JS",
  "side is checked on inputs CuTe itself produced.",
  "",
  "atom_smem / atom_tiler build the ATOM over a smaller box than the tile being",
  "partitioned, which is the only way to reach TMA_Iter > 1. That regime matters:",
  "it is where mode 1 of composition(tile, layout_V) comes out HIERARCHICAL, and so",
  "the only place the Shape<Shape<_1,_1>> coalesce profile is distinguishable from a",
  "rank-1 one. Without such a case the profile constant is untested. When they are",
  "absent the atom is built over the tile itself, as in ordinary single-shot usage."
 ],
