 "_comment_local_tile": [
  "local_tile(tensor, tiler, coord[, proj]) -- zipped_divide plus a slice, and,",
  "with a fourth argument, dice(proj, tiler) / dice(proj, coord) before that.",
  "The oracle is cute.local_tile itself, run over a real Tensor: the result LAYOUT",
  "is diffed pointwise as everywhere else, and the tile's POSITION is checked",
  "separately, because a layout structurally cannot carry a constant. For an",
  "ordinary tensor that position is recorded as CuTeDSL's own crd2idx of the tile",
  "origin (which local_tile over make_identity_tensor reports); for a coordinate",
  "(basis-strided) tensor the iterator IS the origin coordinate, read off directly.",
  "'tiler' and 'coord' are the raw strings the tab's fields take -- several lines is",
  "a Tiler tuple, one line with a colon a single layout tiler, one without a Shape",
  "tiler (CLAUDE.md) -- so the parser is exercised on the way in.",
  "An 'equiv' block gives the same call with proj already applied by hand; run.js",
  "requires the two to agree, which turns the tab's claim that proj is nothing but",
  "dicing into something enforced rather than asserted."
 ],
